IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sisr-dates`

-- Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Regulations 1994 (Cth) -- baseline encoding from the seat of the claimant: the fund
-- member who asks for their super to be released or moved (on severe financial hardship, a terminal medical condition, a
-- compassionate ground, a small balance, or after leaving Australia as a former temporary resident), and the child who is
-- paid a death benefit pension from a parent's super.
--
-- SEAT. The member (or, in reg 6.21(2B), the deceased member's child). Questions are phrased as that person asks them. The
-- trustee, the Regulator (the Commissioner of Taxation for reg 6.19A), APRA and the Immigration Department get no seat:
-- their satisfactions and determinations are asked as facts ("the trustee is satisfied that ...").
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list). No question takes a DEONTIC or an
-- EVENT. The two duties with a deadline the member meets (reg 6.20A(4), (5): pay the departing member within 28 days; reg
-- 6.34A(2), (3): roll over within 3 business days, or 30 days) are regulative rules run inside a question.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: regs 6.01(2) ("preservation age"), 6.01(5), (5A), 6.01A, 6.01B, 6.17(2)(b), 6.18(2), 6.19A,
-- 6.20A, 6.20B, 6.21(2B), (2C), 6.33(1), 6.34(2), 6.34A(2)-(6); Schedule 1 Part 1 items 102A, 103A, 104, 105, 107, 111.
-- What is out, and why, is in NOTES.md.
--
-- Edition: Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Regulations 1994, Compilation No. 159, compilation date 1 July 2026
-- (register id F2026C00541), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/F1996B00580.txt.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Answers follow the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05
-- (NOTES.md): JUST FALSE is the text's own no; NOTHING is where the text is silent or limited by its own wording.

§ `Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Regulations 1994 -- the claimant`

DECLARE `Claim party` IS ONE OF `my fund's trustee`, `I, the member`
DECLARE `Claim step` IS ONE OF
    `pay my departing super as a single lump sum`
    `roll over or transfer my withdrawal benefit`

§§ `Preservation age (reg 6.01(2))`

-- reg 6.01(2) "preservation age means: (a) for a person born before 1 July 1960--55 years; (b) ... 1 July 1960 to 30 June
-- 1961--56 years; (c) ... 1 July 1961 to 30 June 1962--57 years; (d) ... 1 July 1962 to 30 June 1963--58 years; (e) ... 1
-- July 1963 to 30 June 1964--59 years; or (f) for a person born after 30 June 1964--60 years."
GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the preservation age of a person born on` `born on` MEANS
    BRANCH IF DATE_SERIAL `born on` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) THEN 55
           IF DATE_SERIAL `born on` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the calendar date` 1 7 1961) THEN 56
           IF DATE_SERIAL `born on` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the calendar date` 1 7 1962) THEN 57
           IF DATE_SERIAL `born on` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the calendar date` 1 7 1963) THEN 58
           IF DATE_SERIAL `born on` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the calendar date` 1 7 1964) THEN 59
           OTHERWISE 60

§§ `Severe financial hardship (reg 6.01(5), (5A); Schedule 1 item 105)`
-- Situation: asked only by a member who is short of money and asks the fund for an early payment.

-- reg 6.01(5)(a): taken to be in severe financial hardship if "the trustee ... is satisfied: (i) based on written evidence
-- provided by at least one Commonwealth department or agency responsible for administering a class of Commonwealth income
-- support payments, that: (A) the person has received Commonwealth income support payments for a continuous period of 26
-- weeks; and (B) the person was in receipt of payments of that kind on the date of the written evidence; and (ii) that the
-- person is unable to meet reasonable and immediate family living expenses".
-- reg 6.01(5A): "The written evidence provided for by paragraph (5)(a) is of no effect if it is dated more than 21 days
-- before the date of the person's application to the trustee". Evidence dated 21 days before the application counts; 22
-- days does not. Evidence dated after the application is not "more than 21 days before" it, and counts.
-- "Commonwealth income support payment" (reg 6.01(2)) excludes austudy and youth allowance for full-time study; the member
-- states whether the payments are of the kind defined.
@export Am I in severe financial hardship on the 26-week income support ground (SIS Regulations reg 6.01(5)(a), (5A))? This ground lets your fund pay you one lump sum of $1,000 to $10,000 in each 12 months.
GIVEN `weeks of continuous income support` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in a row, up to the date of the agency's written evidence, you have received Commonwealth income support payments (for example JobSeeker or a pension; not austudy, and not youth allowance while studying full-time)
      `receiving it on the date of the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were receiving that kind of payment on the date of the agency's written evidence
      `I have the agency's written evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have written evidence of those payments from a Commonwealth department or agency that administers them (for example Services Australia)
      `the date of the evidence` IS A DATE @desc The date of that written evidence
      `the date of my application` IS A DATE @desc The date of your application to the fund for the payment
      `the trustee is satisfied I cannot meet my family living expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund's trustee is satisfied that you are unable to meet reasonable and immediate family living expenses (the trustee's judgment)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in severe financial hardship on the 26-week ground` IF
        `I have the agency's written evidence`
    AND `weeks of continuous income support` AT LEAST 26
    AND `receiving it on the date of the evidence`
    AND `the days from` `the date of the evidence` `to` `the date of my application` AT MOST 21
    AND `the trustee is satisfied I cannot meet my family living expenses`

-- reg 6.01(5)(b): "the person has reached the age that is the person's preservation age plus 39 weeks". 39 weeks is 273
-- days after the day the person reaches preservation age.
@export On what day do I reach my preservation age plus 39 weeks (SIS Regulations reg 6.01(5)(b))? From that day you can ask for your super on the preservation-age ground of severe financial hardship.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day do I reach my preservation age plus 39 weeks` `my date of birth` MEANS
    `the date` 273 `days after` (`the day of reaching age` (`the preservation age of a person born on` `my date of birth`) `if born on` `my date of birth`)

-- reg 6.01(5)(b): "... and the trustee ... is satisfied: (i) based on written evidence provided by at least one Commonwealth
-- department or agency ...--that the person received Commonwealth income support payments for a cumulative period of 39
-- weeks after the person reached the person's preservation age; and (ii) that the person was not gainfully employed on a
-- full-time, or part-time, basis on the date of the application". The age is read as reached on or before the application.
-- The 21-day rule in (5A) applies only to the evidence for paragraph (a).
@export Am I in severe financial hardship on the preservation-age ground (SIS Regulations reg 6.01(5)(b))? This ground lets your fund pay you your preserved super in any form, with no cap.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date of my application` IS A DATE @desc The date of your application to the fund for the payment
      `weeks of income support since my preservation age` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in all (they need not be in a row) you have received Commonwealth income support payments since you reached your preservation age
      `I have the agency's written evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have written evidence of those payments from a Commonwealth department or agency that administers them (for example Services Australia)
      `I was working on the date of my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were gainfully employed, full-time or part-time, on the date of your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in severe financial hardship on the preservation-age ground` IF
        `the day` (`On what day do I reach my preservation age plus 39 weeks` `my date of birth`) `is on or before` `the date of my application`
    AND `I have the agency's written evidence`
    AND `weeks of income support since my preservation age` AT LEAST 39
    AND (NOT `I was working on the date of my application`)

DECLARE `Hardship ground` IS ONE OF
    `the 26-week income support ground (reg 6.01(5)(a))`
    `the preservation-age ground (reg 6.01(5)(b))`

-- Schedule 1 item 105, column 3: "For a person taken to be in severe financial hardship under paragraph 6.01(5)(a)--in each
-- 12 month period (beginning on the date of first payment), a single lump sum not less than $1,000 (except if the amount of
-- the person's preserved benefits and restricted non-preserved benefits is less than that amount) and not more than
-- $10,000. For a person taken to be in severe financial hardship under paragraph 6.01(5)(b)--Nil."
-- reg 6.18(2): the amount cashed "must not exceed ... the amount of preserved benefits of the member that had accrued at the
-- time when the member satisfied the condition of release". The balance asked is taken as that amount.
-- The 12-month period is read as running from the payment that began it: a payment under (a) opens a period, and the next
-- may be paid from the same day 12 months on (fork register: the other reading counts fixed years from the very first
-- payment).
GIVEN `paid before` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date of my latest payment` IS A DATE, `the date of this payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new 12-month period has begun` IF
        (NOT `paid before`)
    OR  `the day` (`the same day` 12 `months after` `the date of my latest payment`) `is on or before` `the date of this payment`

@export What is the most my fund may pay me now for severe financial hardship (SIS Regulations Schedule 1 item 105, reg 6.18(2))? On the 26-week ground it is one lump sum of up to $10,000 in each 12 months; on the preservation-age ground it is your whole preserved and restricted non-preserved balance.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Hardship ground` @desc The ground you meet: "the 26-week income support ground (reg 6.01(5)(a))" or "the preservation-age ground (reg 6.01(5)(b))"
      `my balance` IS A NUMBER @desc Your preserved and restricted non-preserved benefits in the fund, in dollars
      `paid before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this fund has already paid you a lump sum on the 26-week ground
      `the date of my latest payment` IS A DATE @desc The date of the latest such payment (any date if none)
      `the date of this payment` IS A DATE @desc The date of the payment you are asking for now
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my fund may pay me now for severe financial hardship` `the ground` `my balance` `paid before` `the date of my latest payment` `the date of this payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the preservation-age ground (reg 6.01(5)(b))` THEN `my balance`
    WHEN `the 26-week income support ground (reg 6.01(5)(a))` THEN
        IF `a new 12-month period has begun` `paid before` `the date of my latest payment` `the date of this payment`
        THEN
            IF `my balance` LESS THAN 10000
            THEN `my balance`
            ELSE 10000
        ELSE 0

-- The same, for one proposed lump sum: JUST TRUE if item 105 and reg 6.18(2) allow it, JUST FALSE if they do not (reg
-- 6.17(2)(b): benefits "must not be paid ... except when, and to the extent that" this Part permits). Below $1,000 on the
-- 26-week ground is allowed only where the balance itself is below $1,000 (then any amount up to the balance; fork register).
@export May my fund pay me this lump sum for severe financial hardship (SIS Regulations Schedule 1 item 105, regs 6.17(2), 6.18(2))?
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Hardship ground` @desc The ground you meet: "the 26-week income support ground (reg 6.01(5)(a))" or "the preservation-age ground (reg 6.01(5)(b))"
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The lump sum you are asking for, in dollars
      `my balance` IS A NUMBER @desc Your preserved and restricted non-preserved benefits in the fund, in dollars
      `paid before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this fund has already paid you a lump sum on the 26-week ground
      `the date of my latest payment` IS A DATE @desc The date of the latest such payment (any date if none)
      `the date of this payment` IS A DATE @desc The date of the payment you are asking for now
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my fund pay me this lump sum for severe financial hardship` `the ground` `the amount` `my balance` `paid before` `the date of my latest payment` `the date of this payment` MEANS
    JUST (    `the amount` GREATER THAN 0
          AND `the amount` AT MOST `What is the most my fund may pay me now for severe financial hardship` `the ground` `my balance` `paid before` `the date of my latest payment` `the date of this payment`
          AND `the floor is met`)
    WHERE
        `the floor is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the ground`
            WHEN `the preservation-age ground (reg 6.01(5)(b))` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the 26-week income support ground (reg 6.01(5)(a))` THEN
                `my balance` LESS THAN 1000 OR `the amount` AT LEAST 1000

§§ `Terminal medical condition (reg 6.01A; Schedule 1 item 102A)`
-- Situation: asked only by a member who has been told they have an illness or injury likely to cause death.

-- reg 6.01A: "a terminal medical condition exists in relation to a person at a particular time if ... (a) two registered
-- medical practitioners have certified, jointly or separately, that the person suffers from an illness, or has incurred an
-- injury, that is likely to result in the death of the person within a period (the certification period) that ends not
-- more than 24 months after the date of the certification; (b) at least one of the registered medical practitioners is a
-- specialist practicing in an area related to the illness or injury suffered by the person; (c) either: (i) if there is
-- one certification period--the certification period has not ended; or (ii) otherwise--neither of the certification
-- periods has ended." The period has not ended on its own last day. Item 102A: cashing restriction "Nil".
GIVEN `certified on` IS A DATE, `the period ends on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certification period is within 24 months` IF
        `the day` `the period ends on` `is on or before` (`the same day` 24 `months after` `certified on`)
    AND (NOT (`the day` `certified on` `is after` `the period ends on`))

@export Do I have a terminal medical condition on this day (SIS Regulations reg 6.01A)? If you do, you can take all your super in any form (Schedule 1 item 102A).
GIVEN `both are registered medical practitioners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both doctors who certified are registered medical practitioners
      `one is a specialist in a related area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one of them is a specialist practising in an area related to your illness or injury
      `they certified jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the two doctors gave one joint certificate (true) or two separate certificates (false)
      `the first certificate's date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the joint certificate, or of the first doctor's certificate
      `the first certification period ends on` IS A DATE @desc The day by which that certificate says you are likely to die (the end of its certification period)
      `the second certificate's date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the second doctor's certificate (ignored for a joint certificate)
      `the second certification period ends on` IS A DATE @desc The end of the second certificate's certification period (ignored for a joint certificate)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a terminal medical condition on this day` IF
        `both are registered medical practitioners`
    AND `one is a specialist in a related area`
    AND `the certification period is within 24 months` `the first certificate's date` `the first certification period ends on`
    AND (NOT (`the day` `the first certificate's date` `is after` `the day asked about`))
    AND `the day` `the day asked about` `is on or before` `the first certification period ends on`
    AND (    `they certified jointly`
         OR  (    `the certification period is within 24 months` `the second certificate's date` `the second certification period ends on`
              AND (NOT (`the day` `the second certificate's date` `is after` `the day asked about`))
              AND `the day` `the day asked about` `is on or before` `the second certification period ends on`))

-- The last day on which the condition exists on these certificates: the end of the (earlier) certification period. NOTHING
-- where the certificates do not meet (a) and (b), so that no condition exists on them at all.
@export Until what day does my terminal medical condition last on these certificates (SIS Regulations reg 6.01A(c))?
GIVEN `both are registered medical practitioners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both doctors who certified are registered medical practitioners
      `one is a specialist in a related area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one of them is a specialist practising in an area related to your illness or injury
      `they certified jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the two doctors gave one joint certificate (true) or two separate certificates (false)
      `the first certificate's date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the joint certificate, or of the first doctor's certificate
      `the first certification period ends on` IS A DATE @desc The day by which that certificate says you are likely to die (the end of its certification period)
      `the second certificate's date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the second doctor's certificate (ignored for a joint certificate)
      `the second certification period ends on` IS A DATE @desc The end of the second certificate's certification period (ignored for a joint certificate)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Until what day does my terminal medical condition last` `both are registered medical practitioners` `one is a specialist in a related area` `they certified jointly` `the first certificate's date` `the first certification period ends on` `the second certificate's date` `the second certification period ends on` MEANS
    IF `both are registered medical practitioners` AND `one is a specialist in a related area` AND `the certificates are in time`
    THEN
        IF `they certified jointly`
        THEN JUST `the first certification period ends on`
        ELSE JUST (`the earlier of` `the first certification period ends on` `and` `the second certification period ends on`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the certificates are in time` MEANS
                `the certification period is within 24 months` `the first certificate's date` `the first certification period ends on`
            AND (    `they certified jointly`
                 OR  `the certification period is within 24 months` `the second certificate's date` `the second certification period ends on`)

§§ `Release on compassionate grounds (reg 6.19A; Schedule 1 item 107)`
-- Situation: asked only by a member who applies to the Regulator (the Commissioner of Taxation) for an early release to
-- meet one of the listed expenses.

DECLARE `Compassionate ground` IS ONE OF
    `medical treatment for me or a dependant (reg 6.19A(1)(a))`
    `medical transport for me or a dependant (reg 6.19A(1)(a))`
    `a loan payment to stop the mortgagee foreclosing on or selling my home (reg 6.19A(1)(b))`
    `modifying my home or vehicle for a severe disability (reg 6.19A(1)(c))`
    `my palliative care (reg 6.19A(1)(d))`
    `a dependant's palliative care, death, funeral or burial (reg 6.19A(1)(e))`
    `another case consistent with those grounds, as the Regulator determines (reg 6.19A(1)(f))`

-- reg 6.19A(2): "The Regulator must determine, in writing, that the person has satisfied ... a condition of release on a
-- compassionate ground if the Regulator is satisfied that: (a) the release is required on a ground mentioned in subregulation
-- (1); and (b) the person does not have the financial capacity to meet an expense arising from that ground."
-- (3): "The Regulator cannot be satisfied that money is required for medical treatment unless 2 registered medical
-- practitioners (at least one of whom must be a specialist) certify that: (a) the medical treatment is necessary to: (i)
-- treat a life threatening illness or injury; or (ii) alleviate acute, or chronic, pain; or (iii) alleviate an acute, or
-- chronic, mental disturbance; and (b) the treatment is not readily available ... through the public health system."
-- (4): medical transport only if the treatment it is for "has been certified, under subregulation (3)".
-- (5): the mortgage ground only if "the person gives to the Regulator a written statement from the mortgagee that: (a)
-- payment of an amount is overdue; and (b) if the person fails to pay the amount, the mortgagee will: (i) foreclose ...; or
-- (ii) exercise its ... power of sale"; (6): the statement "must include" 3 months' repayments and 12 months' interest.
-- JUST TRUE: the Regulator must determine that I have met the condition of release. JUST FALSE: (3), (4) or (5) bars it
-- ("cannot be satisfied ... unless"), or the Regulator is not satisfied of (2)(a) and (b) (an "if" condition). A mortgagee's
-- statement without the (6) figures is read as not a statement under (5) (fork register).
@export Must the Regulator release my super on this compassionate ground (SIS Regulations reg 6.19A(2)-(6))? The Regulator (the Commissioner of Taxation) must determine that you have met a condition of release if satisfied that the release is required on the ground and that you cannot otherwise meet the expense.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Compassionate ground` @desc The ground you rely on, one of the listed grounds in reg 6.19A(1)
      `two doctors, one a specialist, certified the treatment is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For medical treatment or transport: whether two registered medical practitioners, at least one a specialist, certified that the treatment is necessary to treat a life-threatening illness or injury, or to alleviate acute or chronic pain or an acute or chronic mental disturbance
      `they certified it is not readily available in the public system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For medical treatment or transport: whether they also certified that the treatment is not readily available to you (or the dependant) through the public health system
      `I have the mortgagee's written statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the mortgage ground: whether you have given the Regulator a written statement from the mortgagee that a payment is overdue and that, if it is not paid, the mortgagee will foreclose on or sell your principal place of residence
      `the statement gives the repayments and interest figures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the mortgage ground: whether that statement gives the amount of 3 months' repayments and of 12 months' interest on the outstanding balance
      `the Regulator is satisfied the release is required on the ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Regulator is satisfied that the release is required on this ground (for the last ground, that the Regulator determines your case is consistent with the listed grounds)
      `the Regulator is satisfied I cannot meet the expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Regulator is satisfied that you do not have the financial capacity to meet the expense
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the Regulator release my super on this compassionate ground` `the ground` `two doctors, one a specialist, certified the treatment is necessary` `they certified it is not readily available in the public system` `I have the mortgagee's written statement` `the statement gives the repayments and interest figures` `the Regulator is satisfied the release is required on the ground` `the Regulator is satisfied I cannot meet the expense` MEANS
    IF `the evidence the regulation demands is there`
    THEN JUST (`the Regulator is satisfied the release is required on the ground` AND `the Regulator is satisfied I cannot meet the expense`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the medical certificates are there` MEANS
            `two doctors, one a specialist, certified the treatment is necessary` AND `they certified it is not readily available in the public system`
        `the evidence the regulation demands is there` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the ground`
            WHEN `medical treatment for me or a dependant (reg 6.19A(1)(a))` THEN `the medical certificates are there`
            WHEN `medical transport for me or a dependant (reg 6.19A(1)(a))` THEN `the medical certificates are there`
            WHEN `a loan payment to stop the mortgagee foreclosing on or selling my home (reg 6.19A(1)(b))` THEN
                `I have the mortgagee's written statement` AND `the statement gives the repayments and interest figures`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Schedule 1 item 107, column 3: "A single lump sum, not exceeding an amount determined, in writing, by the Regulator, being
-- an amount that: (a) taking account of the ground and of the person's financial capacity, is reasonably required; and (b)
-- in the case of the ground mentioned in paragraph 6.19A(1)(b)--in each 12 month period (beginning on the date of first
-- payment), does not exceed an amount equal to the sum of: (i) 3 months' repayments; and (ii) 12 months' interest on the
-- outstanding balance of the loan". The amount the Regulator determined is asked; on the mortgage ground it is cut to what is
-- left of the (b) cap in the current 12-month period.
@export What is the most my fund may pay me on the Regulator's compassionate-ground determination (SIS Regulations Schedule 1 item 107)? It is one lump sum, no more than the amount the Regulator determined; for a mortgage, no more in each 12 months than 3 months' repayments plus 12 months' interest.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Compassionate ground` @desc The ground the Regulator's determination is on
      `the amount the Regulator determined` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, that the Regulator's written determination says may be released
      `three months' repayments` IS A NUMBER @desc For the mortgage ground: 3 months' repayments under the mortgage, in dollars
      `twelve months' interest` IS A NUMBER @desc For the mortgage ground: 12 months' interest on the outstanding balance of the loan, in dollars
      `already paid in this 12-month period` IS A NUMBER @desc For the mortgage ground: how much has already been paid to you on that ground in the current 12-month period, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my fund may pay me on the compassionate-ground determination` `the ground` `the amount the Regulator determined` `three months' repayments` `twelve months' interest` `already paid in this 12-month period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `a loan payment to stop the mortgagee foreclosing on or selling my home (reg 6.19A(1)(b))` THEN
        IF `the amount the Regulator determined` LESS THAN `what is left of the cap`
        THEN `the amount the Regulator determined`
        ELSE `what is left of the cap`
    OTHERWISE `the amount the Regulator determined`
    WHERE
        `the room under the cap` MEANS (`three months' repayments` PLUS `twelve months' interest`) MINUS `already paid in this 12-month period`
        `what is left of the cap` MEANS
            IF `the room under the cap` LESS THAN 0
            THEN 0
            ELSE `the room under the cap`

§§ `Small balances (Schedule 1 items 104 and 111)`
-- Situation: asked only by a member who has left a job, or who was a lost member and has been found.

DECLARE `Small balance occasion` IS ONE OF
    `I left a job with a standard employer-sponsor of the fund (item 104)`
    `I was a lost member and have been found (item 111)`

-- Item 104: "Termination of gainful employment with a standard employer-sponsor of the regulated superannuation fund on or
-- after 1 July 1997 (where the member's preserved benefits in the fund at the time of the termination are less than $200)":
-- Nil. Item 111: "Being a lost member who is found, and the value of whose benefit in the fund, when released, is less than
-- $200": Nil. $200 itself is not less than $200. A job that ended before 1 July 1997 is outside item 104 (FALSE for that
-- item; other conditions of release are not asked here).
@export Can I take my preserved super in full because the balance is under $200 (SIS Regulations Schedule 1 items 104, 111)?
GIVEN `the occasion` IS A `Small balance occasion` @desc Which occasion applies: you left a job with an employer that sponsors the fund, or you were a lost member and have been found
      `the balance` IS A NUMBER @desc For item 104: your preserved benefits in the fund when the job ended; for item 111: the value of your benefit when it is released; in dollars
      `the day the job ended` IS A DATE @desc For item 104: the day your employment with that employer ended (any date for item 111)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I take my preserved super in full because the balance is under 200 dollars` IF
        `the balance` LESS THAN 200
    AND `the date rule is met`
    WHERE
        `the date rule is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the occasion`
            WHEN `I left a job with a standard employer-sponsor of the fund (item 104)` THEN
                (NOT (`the day` (`the calendar date` 1 7 1997) `is after` `the day the job ended`))
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Temporary residents and departing Australia (regs 6.01B, 6.20A, 6.20B; Schedule 1 item 103A)`
-- Situation: asked only by a member who holds or held a temporary visa.

-- reg 6.01B(1): "This regulation applies to a member who is or was a temporary resident." (2): "does not apply to a member
-- who: (a) is an Australian citizen, a New Zealand citizen or a permanent resident; or (b) is, at any time, the holder of a
-- Subclass 405 (Investor Retirement) visa or a Subclass 410 (Retirement) visa".
@export Am I limited to the temporary residents' conditions of release (SIS Regulations reg 6.01B(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I hold or held a temporary visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, or were, the holder of a temporary visa under the Migration Act 1958
      `I am a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, a New Zealand citizen, or the holder of a permanent visa that is still in effect
      `I have held a 405 or 410 retirement visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever held a Subclass 405 (Investor Retirement) or Subclass 410 (Retirement) visa
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I limited to the temporary residents' conditions of release` IF
        `I hold or held a temporary visa`
    AND (NOT `I am a citizen or permanent resident`)
    AND (NOT `I have held a 405 or 410 retirement visa`)

DECLARE `Condition of release` IS ONE OF
    `retirement (item 101)`
    `death (item 102)`
    `terminal medical condition (item 102A)`
    `permanent incapacity (item 103)`
    `former temporary resident asking in writing for release after leaving Australia (item 103A)`
    `the trustee must or may pay the Commissioner of Taxation for unclaimed money (item 103B)`
    `leaving a job with a standard employer-sponsor, preserved balance under 200 dollars (item 104)`
    `severe financial hardship (item 105)`
    `attaining age 65 (item 106)`
    `the Regulator's compassionate-ground determination (item 107)`
    `the Regulator's coronavirus compassionate-ground determination (item 107A)`
    `leaving a job with an employer who contributed for me (item 108)`
    `temporary incapacity (item 109)`
    `acquiring a deferred superannuation income stream (item 109A)`
    `attaining preservation age (item 110)`
    `a lost member found, balance under 200 dollars (item 111)`
    `a Commissioner of Taxation release authority (item 111A)`
    `a release authority I give under section 135-40 (item 111B)`
    `a transitional release authority (item 113)`
    `moving permanently to New Zealand and nominating a KiwiSaver scheme (item 113A)`
    `a condition in an approval under the Act s 62(1)(b)(v) (item 114)`

-- reg 6.01B(3): "The only conditions of release that can be satisfied in respect of a member to whom this regulation applies
-- are: (a) a condition of release that was satisfied by the member before 1 April 2009; and (b) the conditions of release in
-- items 102, 102A, 103, 103A, 103B, 107A, 109, 111A, 111B, 113A ... of Schedule 1." A closed list ("the only"): TRUE where
-- it shuts the condition out, FALSE where it does not. Severe financial hardship (105) and the reg 6.19A compassionate
-- ground (107) are not on the list.
@export Does the temporary residents' rule stop me meeting this condition of release (SIS Regulations reg 6.01B(3))?
GIVEN `I hold or held a temporary visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, or were, the holder of a temporary visa under the Migration Act 1958
      `I am a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, a New Zealand citizen, or the holder of a permanent visa that is still in effect
      `I have held a 405 or 410 retirement visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever held a Subclass 405 (Investor Retirement) or Subclass 410 (Retirement) visa
      `the condition` IS A `Condition of release` @desc The condition of release in Schedule 1 Part 1 you want to rely on
      `I met it before 1 April 2009` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you met that condition of release before 1 April 2009
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the temporary residents' rule stop me meeting this condition of release` IF
        `Am I limited to the temporary residents' conditions of release` `I hold or held a temporary visa` `I am a citizen or permanent resident` `I have held a 405 or 410 retirement visa`
    AND (NOT `I met it before 1 April 2009`)
    AND (NOT `on the list`)
    WHERE
        `on the list` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the condition`
            WHEN `death (item 102)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `terminal medical condition (item 102A)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `permanent incapacity (item 103)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `former temporary resident asking in writing for release after leaving Australia (item 103A)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the trustee must or may pay the Commissioner of Taxation for unclaimed money (item 103B)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the Regulator's coronavirus compassionate-ground determination (item 107A)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `temporary incapacity (item 109)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a Commissioner of Taxation release authority (item 111A)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a release authority I give under section 135-40 (item 111B)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `moving permanently to New Zealand and nominating a KiwiSaver scheme (item 113A)` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `What my fund must do with my departing request` IS ONE OF
    `my fund must pay me my withdrawal benefit as a lump sum within 28 days after my request was lodged (reg 6.20A)`
    `my fund may pay me, but need not, because it is an unfunded public sector scheme (reg 6.20B)`
    `reg 6.20A and reg 6.20B do not require or allow payment on these facts`

-- reg 6.20A(1): applies "if: (a) the member: (i) was a temporary resident; and (ii) is not an Australian citizen, New Zealand
-- citizen or permanent resident; and (iii) has left Australia; and (b) the member's visa has ceased to be in effect."
-- (1A): "The member's benefits must be cashed if: (a) the trustee ... receives a request from the member ...; and (b)
-- subregulation (2) or (3) is complied with." (2): "If the member's withdrawal benefit in the fund is less than $5 000, the
-- trustee ... must receive: (a) a copy, or other evidence, of a visa showing that the member was a temporary resident but
-- the member's temporary visa has ceased to be in effect; and (b) a copy of the member's passport showing that the member
-- has left Australia." (3): "The trustee ... must be satisfied, based on a written statement from the Immigration
-- Department, that" the same two things. Route (2) is open only below $5,000; route (3) at any balance.
-- reg 6.20B: the same for an unfunded public sector superannuation scheme, but "may be cashed".
@export Must my fund pay out my super now that I have left Australia (SIS Regulations regs 6.20A, 6.20B)? A former temporary resident whose visa has ended, who has left Australia and asks in writing, must be paid the withdrawal benefit within 28 days.
GIVEN `I was a temporary resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held a temporary visa under the Migration Act 1958
      `I am a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, a New Zealand citizen, or a permanent resident
      `I have left Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have left Australia
      `my visa has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your visa has ceased to be in effect
      `I have asked the fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund's trustee has received your request to cash your benefits
      `my withdrawal benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your withdrawal benefit in the fund, in dollars
      `I gave copies of my visa evidence and passport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee has received a copy or other evidence of your visa showing the temporary visa has ceased, and a copy of your passport showing you have left Australia
      `the trustee is satisfied on the Immigration Department's statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee is satisfied, on a written statement from the Immigration Department, that your temporary visa has ceased and you have left Australia
      `my fund is an unfunded public sector scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your fund is an unfunded public sector superannuation scheme
GIVETH A `What my fund must do with my departing request`
`Must my fund pay out my super now that I have left Australia` `I was a temporary resident` `I am a citizen or permanent resident` `I have left Australia` `my visa has ceased` `I have asked the fund` `my withdrawal benefit` `I gave copies of my visa evidence and passport` `the trustee is satisfied on the Immigration Department's statement` `my fund is an unfunded public sector scheme` MEANS
    IF `the regulation applies` AND `I have asked the fund` AND `the evidence is in`
    THEN
        IF `my fund is an unfunded public sector scheme`
        THEN `my fund may pay me, but need not, because it is an unfunded public sector scheme (reg 6.20B)`
        ELSE `my fund must pay me my withdrawal benefit as a lump sum within 28 days after my request was lodged (reg 6.20A)`
    ELSE `reg 6.20A and reg 6.20B do not require or allow payment on these facts`
    WHERE
        `the regulation applies` MEANS
                `I was a temporary resident`
            AND (NOT `I am a citizen or permanent resident`)
            AND `I have left Australia`
            AND `my visa has ceased`
        `the evidence is in` MEANS
                (`my withdrawal benefit` LESS THAN 5000 AND `I gave copies of my visa evidence and passport`)
            OR  `the trustee is satisfied on the Immigration Department's statement`

-- reg 6.20A(4): "The benefits must be cashed in the period mentioned in subregulation (5): (a) as a single lump sum that is at
-- least the amount of the member's withdrawal benefit"; (5)(b): "28 days after the request is lodged" (a request lodged by
-- 31 October 2002 had 3 months; not encoded). The last day is the 28th day after the day the request was lodged.
@export By when must my fund pay my super after I have left Australia (SIS Regulations reg 6.20A(4), (5))? Within 28 days after your request was lodged.
GIVEN `lodged on` IS A DATE @desc The day your request to the fund was lodged
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my fund pay my departing super` `lodged on` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `lodged on`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim step`
`reg 6.20A -- my fund must pay my departing super within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `my fund's trustee`
    MUST `pay my departing super as a single lump sum`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `my fund's trustee` BECAUSE "the withdrawal benefit was not cashed within 28 days after the request was lodged (reg 6.20A(4), (5))"

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6.20A -- a payment on this day is in time` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `reg 6.20A -- my fund must pay my departing super within 28 days` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `my fund's trustee` `pay my departing super as a single lump sum` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where my payment or rollover stands` IS ONE OF
    `made in time`
    `not yet made, and not yet late`
    `late: not made by the last day the regulation allows`
    `the regulation sets no last day on these facts`

@export I have left Australia and asked my fund for my super: has it paid in time (SIS Regulations reg 6.20A(4), (5))? Assumes your fund must pay you (see the question on whether it must).
GIVEN `lodged on` IS A DATE @desc The day your request to the fund was lodged
      `paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund has paid you the lump sum
      `paid on` IS A DATE @desc The day it paid (any date if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where my payment or rollover stands`
`Has my fund paid my departing super in time` `lodged on` `paid` `paid on` `today` MEANS
    IF `paid`
    THEN
        IF `reg 6.20A -- a payment on this day is in time` (`the days from` `lodged on` `to` `paid on`)
        THEN `made in time`
        ELSE `late: not made by the last day the regulation allows`
    ELSE
        IF `the day` `today` `is on or before` (`By when must my fund pay my departing super` `lodged on`)
        THEN `not yet made, and not yet late`
        ELSE `late: not made by the last day the regulation allows`

§§ `Moving my super to another fund (regs 6.33, 6.34, 6.34A)`
-- Situation: asked only by a member who has asked to roll over or transfer their super.

-- reg 6.33(1): "A member ... may request, in writing, that the whole or a part of the member's withdrawal benefit in the
-- transferring fund be rolled over or transferred". reg 6.34(2): once the request and the information in 6.34(1)(b)-(e)
-- are in, "the trustee must roll over or transfer the amount in accordance with the request".
-- reg 6.34A(2): "as soon as practicable, but in any case not later than 3 business days after: (a) the trustee received the
-- rollover or transfer request; or (b) if the trustee seeks further information under regulation 6.33C or subregulation
-- 6.33D(4) or 6.33E(3)--the date the trustee receives the information". (3): where the receiving fund cannot receive it under
-- the data and payment standards, "not later than 30 days after". (4): where the member made an investment choice, the 3
-- business days may be displaced by redemption steps, but the amount must go "in any case not later than 30 days after";
-- the outer 30 days is the answer given (fork register).
-- (5), (6): an illiquid investment the member was told about (before 1 July 2008) or consented in writing to (with an
-- investment choice) lifts the periods in (2)-(4): no last day then (NOTHING).
-- Not encoded: an APRA suspension or variation under regs 6.36, 6.37 ((2)(c)); the refusals in reg 6.35.
@export By when must my old fund roll over or transfer my super (SIS Regulations reg 6.34A)? Usually within 3 business days after it has your request and any further information it asked for.
GIVEN `the day the fund received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day the fund you are leaving received your request (with the information the approved form requires)
      `the fund asked me for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund asked you for further information under reg 6.33C, 6.33D(4) or 6.33E(3)
      `the day it received that information` IS A DATE @desc The day it received that information (any date if it asked for none)
      `the new fund can receive under the standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund you are moving to can receive the rollover under the superannuation data and payment standards (true for almost every large fund; your fund will say if not)
      `I made an investment choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you chose an investment option in the fund (an investment choice under reg 4.02, 4.02A or 4.02AA)
      `I accepted a longer period for an illiquid investment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consented in writing, when choosing an illiquid investment, that the rollover may take longer than 30 days (or, for an investment held before 1 July 2007, were told so before 1 July 2008)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must my old fund roll over my super` `the day the fund received my request` `the fund asked me for more information` `the day it received that information` `the new fund can receive under the standards` `I made an investment choice` `I accepted a longer period for an illiquid investment` MEANS
    IF `I accepted a longer period for an illiquid investment`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the new fund can receive under the standards` AND (NOT `I made an investment choice`)
        THEN JUST (`the business day` 3 `after` `the start`)
        ELSE JUST (`the date` 30 `days after` `the start`)
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS
            IF `the fund asked me for more information`
            THEN `the day it received that information`
            ELSE `the day the fund received my request`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim step`
`reg 6.34A -- my fund must roll over my super in time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `my fund's trustee`
    MUST `roll over or transfer my withdrawal benefit`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `my fund's trustee` BECAUSE "the amount was not rolled over or transferred within the period in reg 6.34A"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6.34A -- a rollover on this day is in time` `the days allowed` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`reg 6.34A -- my fund must roll over my super in time` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `my fund's trustee` `roll over or transfer my withdrawal benefit` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export I asked my fund to roll over my super: has it done so in time (SIS Regulations reg 6.34A)?
GIVEN `the day the fund received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day the fund you are leaving received your request (with the information the approved form requires)
      `the fund asked me for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund asked you for further information under reg 6.33C, 6.33D(4) or 6.33E(3)
      `the day it received that information` IS A DATE @desc The day it received that information (any date if it asked for none)
      `the new fund can receive under the standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund you are moving to can receive the rollover under the superannuation data and payment standards
      `I made an investment choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you chose an investment option in the fund (an investment choice under reg 4.02, 4.02A or 4.02AA)
      `I accepted a longer period for an illiquid investment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consented in writing that the rollover of an illiquid investment may take longer than 30 days
      `rolled over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund has rolled over or transferred the amount
      `rolled over on` IS A DATE @desc The day it did so (any date if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where my payment or rollover stands`
`Has my old fund rolled over my super in time` `the day the fund received my request` `the fund asked me for more information` `the day it received that information` `the new fund can receive under the standards` `I made an investment choice` `I accepted a longer period for an illiquid investment` `rolled over` `rolled over on` `today` MEANS
    CONSIDER `By when must my old fund roll over my super` `the day the fund received my request` `the fund asked me for more information` `the day it received that information` `the new fund can receive under the standards` `I made an investment choice` `I accepted a longer period for an illiquid investment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the regulation sets no last day on these facts`
    WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN
        IF `rolled over`
        THEN
            IF `reg 6.34A -- a rollover on this day is in time` (`the days from` `the start` `to` `the last day`) (`the days from` `the start` `to` `rolled over on`)
            THEN `made in time`
            ELSE `late: not made by the last day the regulation allows`
        ELSE
            IF `the day` `today` `is on or before` `the last day`
            THEN `not yet made, and not yet late`
            ELSE `late: not made by the last day the regulation allows`
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS
            IF `the fund asked me for more information`
            THEN `the day it received that information`
            ELSE `the day the fund received my request`

§§ `A death benefit pension paid to a child (reg 6.21(2B), (2C))`
-- Situation: asked only by a child of a deceased member who is being paid a death benefit as a pension or annuity.

-- reg 6.21(2C): "This subregulation applies to a person with disability that: (a) is attributable to an intellectual,
-- psychiatric, sensory or physical impairment or a combination of such impairments; and (b) is permanent or likely to be
-- permanent; and (c) results in: (i) a substantially reduced capacity of the person for communication, learning or mobility;
-- and (ii) the need for ongoing support services."
@export Do I have a disability of the kind that lets me keep a death benefit pension past 25 (SIS Regulations reg 6.21(2C))?
GIVEN `it comes from an impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disability is attributable to an intellectual, psychiatric, sensory or physical impairment, or a combination of them
      `it is permanent or likely to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is permanent or likely to be permanent
      `it substantially reduces my capacity for communication, learning or mobility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it results in a substantially reduced capacity for communication, learning or mobility
      `I need ongoing support services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it results in the need for ongoing support services
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a reg 6.21(2C) disability` IF
        `it comes from an impairment`
    AND `it is permanent or likely to be`
    AND `it substantially reduces my capacity for communication, learning or mobility`
    AND `I need ongoing support services`

-- reg 6.21(2B): "If benefits ... are being paid to a child of the deceased member in the form of a pension or an annuity ...,
-- the benefits must be cashed as a lump sum on the earlier of: (a) the day on which the annuity or pension is commuted, or the
-- term of the annuity or pension expires (unless the benefit is rolled over to commence a new annuity or pension); and (b)
-- the day on which the child attains age 25; unless the child is a person with disability to whom subregulation (2C) applies
-- on the day that would otherwise be applicable". With a (2C) disability on that day the answer is NOTHING: the "unless" is
-- met and the regulation sets no day (fork register).
@export On what day must my death benefit pension be paid out to me as a lump sum (SIS Regulations reg 6.21(2B))? For a child of the deceased member, on the earlier of the day the pension ends or is commuted and the day you turn 25, unless you then have a disability of the kind in reg 6.21(2C).
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the pension has a known end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the pension or annuity is being commuted, or its term expires, on a known day (without being rolled over to start a new pension or annuity)
      `the day it ends` IS A DATE @desc That day (any date if there is none)
      `I have a reg 6.21(2C) disability on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day the pension would otherwise have to be paid out, you have a permanent disability from an impairment that substantially reduces your capacity for communication, learning or mobility and needs ongoing support services
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`On what day must my death benefit pension be paid out as a lump sum` `my date of birth` `the pension has a known end` `the day it ends` `I have a reg 6.21(2C) disability on that day` MEANS
    IF `I have a reg 6.21(2C) disability on that day`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the pension has a known end`
        THEN JUST (`the earlier of` `the day it ends` `and` `my 25th birthday`)
        ELSE JUST `my 25th birthday`
    WHERE
        `my 25th birthday` MEANS `the day of reaching age` 25 `if born on` `my date of birth`
